  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Rohde and Schwarz Usa obligated $421M in FY2026 to date across 63 awards, with an average award size of $6.7M. Rohde and Schwarz Usa obligations are up 233.4% year over year. Rohde and Schwarz Usa received the bulk of FY2026 to date obligations from the Department of Transportation, which obligated $403M. Rohde and Schwarz Usa received additional obligations from the Department of Defense, which obligated $16.3M, and smaller amounts from the Department of Commerce, the Department of Homeland Security, and NASA. Rohde and Schwarz Usa recorded major obligations in Telephone Apparatus Manufacturing, which totaled $403M in FY2026 to date. Rohde and Schwarz Usa also had obligations in Instrument Manufacturing for Measuring and Testing Electricity and Electrical Signals ($7.6M), Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing ($7M), and several other NAICS categories with single-line obligations ranging from $1.1M down to $172K. These FY2026 totals are fiscal year to date and represent partial-year obligations rather than full fiscal year totals.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top buyers of Rohde and Schwarz Usa?",
        "body": "The Department of Transportation is the top buyer, obligating $403M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense is the second buyer, obligating $16.3M. The Department of Commerce, the Department of Homeland Security, and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration follow with $852K, $434K, and $251K respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and product lines account for Rohde and Schwarz Usa obligations?",
        "body": "Telephone Apparatus Manufacturing is the largest market, with $403M in FY2026 to date. Instrument Manufacturing for Measuring and Testing Electricity and Electrical Signals accounts for $7.6M and Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing accounts for $7M. Other markets with smaller obligations include Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing ($1.1M) and categories down to Satellite Telecommunications ($172K)."
      }
    ]
  },
